List: Use when you need an ordered collection that can change.
Tuple: Use for fixed data that shouldn't be modified.
Set: Use for unique items and fast membership checks.
Dictionary: Use for storing data as key-value pairs for quick lookups.

Example:

List → ["Amit", "Reni", "Tara"]
Tuple → (12.97, 77.59)
Set → {"python", "sql", "excel"}
Dictionary → {"name": "Reni", "score": 91}